WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.771
Hi there! Who are you?

2
00:00:09.772 --> 00:00:13.639
I'm a flying fox.

3
00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:18.456
We're the biggest kind of bat.

4
00:00:18.457 --> 00:00:21.377
Where do you live?

5
00:00:21.378 --> 00:00:27.067
Most flying foxes live in Asia and Australia.

6
00:00:27.068 --> 00:00:30.768
We move around a lot.

7
00:00:30.769 --> 00:00:36.047
But we like rain forests and swamps.

8
00:00:36.048 --> 00:00:39.361
Do you live alone?

9
00:00:39.362 --> 00:00:41.943
Nope!

10
00:00:41.944 --> 00:00:46.629
Flying foxes live in huge groups.

11
00:00:46.630 --> 00:00:52.454
Some groups have a million flying foxes!

12
00:00:52.455 --> 00:00:55.982
You have big wings!

13
00:00:55.983 --> 00:01:00.240
Yes, our wings are very strong.

14
00:01:00.241 --> 00:01:04.176
We can carry our babies while flying.

15
00:01:04.177 --> 00:01:07.313
Bats sleep in caves, right?

16
00:01:07.314 --> 00:01:10.207
Some bats do.

17
00:01:10.208 --> 00:01:13.992
But we sleep in trees.

18
00:01:13.993 --> 00:01:18.685
We hang upside down from branches.

19
00:01:18.686 --> 00:01:21.286
What do you eat?

20
00:01:21.287 --> 00:01:26.205
Flying foxes mostly eat nectar from flowers.

21
00:01:26.206 --> 00:01:31.445
We also love fruit.

22
00:01:31.446 --> 00:01:34.965
Is it hard to find food?

23
00:01:34.966 --> 00:01:38.490
Not for flying foxes!

24
00:01:38.491 --> 00:01:42.503
We can see really well.

25
00:01:42.504 --> 00:01:49.447
We can also smell things from far away.

26
00:01:49.448 --> 00:01:51.914
The sun is setting.

27
00:01:51.915 --> 00:01:55.543
Time for me to fly!

28
00:01:55.544 --> 00:02:02.297
Good-bye, Flying Fox!

